messages:
kim: Quick report from support: customer hit a 429 on the TS SDK and our sample app just logged Error: request failed. They retried in a tight loop and flooded the backend. We should show a clear path for devs to implement polite retries.

noah: Oof. Do we have the raw response shape? Without retry_after it's hard to backoff properly.

olivia: From proxy: ```{
  "status":429,
  "error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":"Too many requests"},
  "headers":{"retry-after":"10"}
}```

kim: Thanks. TL;DR: SDKs should surface a typed RateLimitError with a helper - not just a generic Error string. Also need docs + a quickstart snippet demonstrating exponential backoff using the provided hint.

noah: Agree. Propose minimal SDK contract: typed errors inheriting RedwoodError, with these fields on the instance: `code` (string), `status` (number), `retryable` (bool), `retry_after` (number | null), `hint` (string | null). Plus helpers `isRetryable()` and `getRetryAfterSec()`.

olivia: That's similar to an earlier convo but I want to emphasize sample apps: show both UI-friendly fallback (show message) and background job retry (automatic). For UI, `hint` should be short and non-technical.

kim: Example snippet for README (TS):
```ts
try {
  await client.generate(...);
} catch (err) {
  if (err.isRetryable && err.isRetryable()) {
    const wait = err.getRetryAfterSec ? err.getRetryAfterSec() : backoff.next();
    await backoff.sleep(wait);
    // retry logic
  } else {
    showToast(err.hint || 'Request failed. Please try again later.');
  }
}
```

noah: Nice. For Python SDK we should do the same but with attributes + `should_retry()` method for parity.

olivia: QA note: add an integration test that fakes a 502 then 200 and asserts client retries when `ServiceUnavailableError.retryable == true`. I'll add a harness test.

kim: Telemetry: emit a dimension `sdk_error_type` with values like `typed_rate_limit`, `typed_service_unavailable`, `generic_error` so we can measure adoption. Add a console metric to the rollout checklist.

noah: Docs change: quickstart page needs a short section "Handling errors" with the snippet and a small table mapping HTTP statuses to SDK exceptions and recommended actions (retryable/do not retry). Olivia can draft.

olivia: I'll write the table and a one-paragraph blurb per error class. Also will sanitize messages so we never leak internal error codes.

devx-bot: PR kim/sdk-error-surface created -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/412 (tests pending) :eyes:

kim: Thanks. Let's aim to ship a minimal parity in both TS + Python next week, then docs + sample app update. Keep this thread for rollout progress.

noah: One last thought: include an opt-in ergonomic layer `client.onError(handler)` in SDKs so apps can register global handlers to centralize UI vs background behavior. That would simplify quickstarts.

olivia: Love it. I'll include an example handler in the sample app PR.

kim: Cool. Action items summarized: (1) TS + Py typed errors + helpers (noah + kim), (2) QA harness tests for retry semantics (olivia), (3) quickstart + sample app updates (olivia), (4) telemetry + console metric (kim).

devx-bot: CI started for PR 412.
